From 01a863baed015006ec46518a03ccd7a30085fa7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stevedamnvan <100538383+stevedamnvan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:36:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] GC-ASSET r17 (gate-ON only): kind check per consumer,
 member-held replay serial; gc_port23 tests all green

- gc_asset_gate.cpp emitted_checked: a token counts only for its own kind (a motion row only for Motion, any other
  row never for Motion), first sight or seen; else why=kind-mismatch. Census on cand-22c6a1c9: none.
- native_model.cpp: a deferred replay of a member-selected part (gc-catalog24b) keeps the queued serial only when
  member_contains(serial, drawn BIN, 64). h2 not-covered 2 -> 1: the last is a room SMD object (identity
  01020018) whose replay falls to the generic GX walker, which carries no proof by design.
- unwired-baseline.json: 0100 source_geometry/unbound-accepted-model 1. SourceGeometry stays unwired.
- gc_asset_members.cpp: weak ensure_disc_catalog (false) for host builds without gc_asset_disc.cpp.
- tests: run_host_tests.sh PASS; python 123 run, OK (6 skipped, was 43 failing). Fixtures updated for the PROF
  probe globals, the registry pack (chunk_count/chunks/mask_geometry), DVD_STAGE/DVD_BORROW_GIVE,
  StdRoom.gca_unused, the world seal; actor-select errors flush the member channel too (24b); explicit
  Rejected/Absent std index and trclass table seal (24b design); kind-mismatch cases. Retired: 2 equivalent
  mutants and 5 reviewed-parent snapshot tests (recipe-ELF knob-off identity replaces them).
Knob-off identity: recipe ELF binary 3bba3367 and 15 overlays identical to out-rr22c6a1crP.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AkGpf8W8oYKd2z6cLgVseU
